ity, excellence, and user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL154: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? cite39†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org .\nL155: \nL156: cite40†Which authors of this paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite41†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL157: \nL158: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite42†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL159: cite43†About†info.arxiv.org · cite44†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite45†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite46†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite47†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite48†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite49†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite50†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L160: \nL161: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2601.09974v1] SPRInG: Continual LLM Personalization via Selective Parametric Adaptation and Retrieval-Interpolated Generation (https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.09974v1)\nciteturn30891view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.09974v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 163\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Artificial Intelligence\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 15 Jan 2026 (this version), latest version 30 Aug 2026 (cite5†v3 )]\nL9: # Title:SPRInG: Continual LLM Personalization via Selective Parametric Adaptation and Retrieval-Interpolated Generation\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Seoyeon Kim , cite7†Jaehyung Kim L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled SPRInG: Continual LLM Personalization via Selective Parametric Adaptation and Retrieval-Interpolated Generation, by Seoyeon Kim and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Personalizing Large Language Models typically relies on static retrieval or one-time adaptation, assuming user preferences remain invariant over time. However, real-world interactions are dynamic, where user interests continuously evolve, posing a challenge for models to adapt to preference drift without catastrophic forgetting.\nL17: Standard continual learning approaches often struggle in this context, as they indiscriminately update on noisy interaction streams, failing to distinguish genuine preference shifts from transient contexts. To address this, we introduce SPRInG, a novel semi-parametric framework designed for effective continual personalization. During training, SPRInG employs drift-driven selective adaptation, which utilizes a likelihood-based scoring function to identify high-novelty interactions.\nL18: This allows the model to selectively update the user-specific adapter on drift signals while preserving hard-to-learn residuals in a replay buffer. During inference, we apply strict relevance gating and fuse parametric knowledge with retrieved history via logit interpolation. Experiments on the long-form personalized generation benchmark demonstrate that SPRInG outperforms existing baselines, validating its robustness for real-world continual personalization.\nL19: Comments:  | under review, 23 pages\nL20: Subjects:  | Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI); Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL21: ACM (Association of Computing Machinery Classification) classes:  | I.2.7\nL22: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:2601.09974 [cs.AI]\nL23:    | (or cite11†arXiv:2601.09974v1 [cs.AI] for this version)\nL24:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2601.09974†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Seoyeon Kim [cite13†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Thu, 1